cal value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ rounded to the nearest integer?" 13194139534150 true] [17592186278855 1113 #uuid "fa37b599-4ad5-59f0-a1aa-7677947192cf" 13194139534150 true] [17592186278855 1145 "Recall that $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x},$ therefore the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=\\frac{4}{5}.\n$$\n\nNow, we have to find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{4}{5})=(53.130\\,1…)^{∘}≈{53.130}^{∘}\n$$\n\nSince ${53.130}^{∘}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={53.130}^{∘}.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the first quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}={53.130}^{∘}.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x>0,$ the second solution must lie in the second quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}={53.130}^{∘}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978818/assets/605af77803fb027c09833b50801fe4b8e6a42a2b623af94a732d0f2f222f9f4a.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$ lies in the $2$nd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={180}^{∘}-{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}-{53.130}^{∘} \\\\  & ={126.870}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x={53.130}^{∘},{126.870}^{∘}.$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}≈53.130\\cdot 126.870≈6\\,741.\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer." 13194139534150 true] [17592186278856 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278857 13194139534150 true] [17592186278856 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278858 13194139534150 true] [17592186278856 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278859 13194139534150 true] [17592186278856 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278860 13194139534150 true] [17592186278856 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278861 13194139534150 true] [17592186278856 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534150 true] [17592186278856 1041 "selection" 13194139534150 true] [17592186278856 1104 #edb/ref 17592186278859 13194139534150 true] [17592186278856 1110 #uuid "b30c3735-b621-50ba-bed0-8145d65b9808" 13194139534150 true] [17592186278857 1034 "4\\,176" 13194139534150 true] [17592186278857 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534150 true] [17592186278857 1111 #uuid "b45c8c7d-4811-5711-a0d2-20dd6d93dd82" 13194139534150 true] [17592186278858 1034 "7\\,641" 13194139534150 true] [17592186278858 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534150 true] [17592186278858 1111 #uuid "7c4dbf3a-7cd9-5861-8948-d0d35f1e1b12" 13194139534150 true] [17592186278859 1034 "6\\,741" 13194139534150 true] [17592186278859 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534150 true] [17592186278859 1111 #uuid "8045ce5e-17fd-56e4-b1f9-e2376449840c" 13194139534150 true] [17592186278860 1034 "4\\,746" 13194139534150 true] [17592186278860 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534150 true] [17592186278860 1111 #uuid "548182d5-ba6c-55ee-b3c0-64aab91113c0" 13194139534150 true] [17592186278861 1034 "1\\,764" 13194139534150 true] [17592186278861 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534150 true] [17592186278861 1111 #uuid "e818ea6a-f98e-5fcf-803e-021b7befa35f" 13194139534150 true] [17592186278862 1017 #edb/ref 17592186278863 13194139534150 true] [17592186278862 1089 "q-338555" 13194139534150 true] [17592186278862 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534150 true] [17592186278862 1100 "The solution to the equation $4\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=3\\operatorname{csc}⁡x-1$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}$ is $x=${{field-1}}${}^{∘}.$" 13194139534150 true] [17592186278862 1113 #uuid "8d26dfe6-88ff-57de-a343-32dc37e76e53" 13194139534150 true] [17592186278862 1145 "First, we rearrange the equation, isolating $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{csc}⁡x & =3\\operatorname{csc}⁡x-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{csc}⁡x & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=-1.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value of $x:$\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-1)=-{90}^{∘}\n$$\n\nNote that $x=-{90}^{∘}$ is not in the given domain. To get a value inside the range, we add ${360}^{∘}:$\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=-{90}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}={270}^{∘}\n$$\n\nAs this is a quadrantal angle, to find the remaining solutions, we use our knowledge of the sine function. We know that the sine function has its minimum values at\n\n$$\nx={270}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nSince the domain $0\\le x<{360}^{∘}$ is one period, and we have already found one minimum value in this period, we conclude that \n$x={270}^{∘}$\nis the only solution." 13194139534150 true] [17592186278863 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278864 13194139534150 true] [17592186278863 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534150 true] [17592186278863 1041 "field-1" 13194139534150 true] [17592186278863 1104 #edb/ref 17592186278864 13194139534150 true] [17592186278863 1110 #uuid "b44fc94a-42bf-5197-9d7c-60c60fb0735d" 13194139534150 true] [17592186278864 1034 "270" 13194139534150 true] [17592186278864 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534150 true] [17592186278864 1111 #uuid "c7f966f9-45cd-5a77-b4cd-91e84bc6aca4" 13194139534150 true] [17592186278865 1017 #edb/ref 17592186278866 13194139534150 true] [17592186278865 1017 #edb/ref 17592186278869 13194139534150 true] [17592186278865 1089 "q-338580" 13194139534150 true] [17592186278865 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534150 true] [17592186278865 1100 "Expressed in **ascending order** in radians, rounded to one decimal place, the solutions to the equation  $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=-\\frac{3}{2},$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi ,$   are\n\n$x≈$\n{{field-1}}, $\\,x≈$\n{{field-2}}." 13194139534150 true] [17592186278865 1113 #uuid "8a2b1492-c6d3-5f3d-bb3b-9d9a623b6acc" 13194139534150 true] [17592186278865 1145 "Recall that $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=-\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{2}{3})=-0.729\\,727…≈-0.7297\n$$\n\nThis value is outside the required domain. To get a value inside the range, we add $2\\pi :$ \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=-0.7297+2\\pi ≈5.5535\n$$\n\nSo,  our first solution is ${x}_{1}=5.5535.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the fourth quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}=0.7297.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}=0.7297.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978818/assets/48d92d2bf48234d7c7aad44936cdefd97f02804383cb7ced2f838661a8c4922a.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$ lies in the $3$rd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\pi +{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi +0.7297 \\\\  & ≈3.8713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, rounded to one decimal place, the solutions are \n\n$$\nx≈3.9,\\,x≈5.6.\n$$" 13194139534150 true] [17592186278866 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278867 13194139534150 true] [17592186278866 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278868 13194139534150 true] [17592186278866 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534150 true] [17592186278866 1041 "field-1" 13194139534150 true] [17592186278866 1104 #edb/ref 17592186278868 13194139534150 true] [17592186278866 1110 #uuid "e72cc9c9-d4cb-5e4d-befa-697e8d50dc70" 13194139534150 true] [17592186278867 1034 "0.7" 13194139534150 true] [17592186278867 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534150 true] [17592186278867 1111 #uuid "0d9e944b-869b-5b71-82fb-2897a29c1cca" 13194139534150 true] [17592186278868 1034 "3.9" 13194139534150 true] [17592186278868 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534150 true] [17592186278868 1111 #uuid "e20ff0a3-9ace-5eaf-8c45-95dfce4b0ee2" 13194139534150 true] [17592186278869 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278870 13194139534150 true] [17592186278869 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534150 true] [17592186278869 1041 "field-2" 13194139534150 true] [17592186278869 1104 #edb/ref 1759218627887