eta }_{R} \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}+{60}^{∘} \\\\  & ={240}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions are $x={300}^{∘},{240}^{∘}.$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=300\\cdot 240=72\\,000.\n$$" 13194139534150 true] [17592186278894 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278895 13194139534150 true] [17592186278894 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278896 13194139534150 true] [17592186278894 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278897 13194139534150 true] [17592186278894 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278898 13194139534150 true] [17592186278894 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278899 13194139534150 true] [17592186278894 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534150 true] [17592186278894 1041 "selection" 13194139534150 true] [17592186278894 1104 #edb/ref 17592186278897 13194139534150 true] [17592186278894 1110 #uuid "5877d332-4979-56f1-bc48-464e8bf007ca" 13194139534150 true] [17592186278895 1034 "36\\,000" 13194139534150 true] [17592186278895 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534150 true] [17592186278895 1111 #uuid "7a22b6eb-4444-5405-9c3b-bc01854115c5" 13194139534150 true] [17592186278896 1034 "7\\,200" 13194139534150 true] [17592186278896 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534150 true] [17592186278896 1111 #uuid "a101926a-c5f5-555b-a6b2-8b9a5ec0d2d6" 13194139534150 true] [17592186278897 1034 "72\\,000" 13194139534150 true] [17592186278897 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534150 true] [17592186278897 1111 #uuid "831f6d5c-8ca2-59da-a1e8-6299be3d14c3" 13194139534150 true] [17592186278898 1034 "28\\,800" 13194139534150 true] [17592186278898 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534150 true] [17592186278898 1111 #uuid "298f201a-369d-5511-96d2-c27e046cb02c" 13194139534150 true] [17592186278899 1034 "3\\,600" 13194139534150 true] [17592186278899 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534150 true] [17592186278899 1111 #uuid "5e28c42e-2442-5c52-8160-2ae0e7b9f5e2" 13194139534150 true] [17592186278900 1017 #edb/ref 17592186278901 13194139534150 true] [17592186278900 1089 "q-77696" 13194139534150 true] [17592186278900 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534150 true] [17592186278900 1100 "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=-\\frac{12}{5}$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi ,$ what is the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ rounded to one decimal place?" 13194139534150 true] [17592186278900 1113 #uuid "f73f66be-93bf-520a-aa38-bdb1e982d68c" 13194139534150 true] [17592186278900 1145 "Recall that $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x},$ therefore the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=-\\frac{5}{12}.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{5}{12})=-0.429\\,775…≈-0.429\\,8\n$$\n\nThis value is outside the required domain. To get a value inside the range, we add $2\\pi .$\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=-0.429\\,8+2\\pi =5.853\\,385…≈5.853\\,4\n$$\n\nOur first solution lies in the fourth quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}=0.429\\,8.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}=0.429\\,8.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978818/assets/912225edc2b860674da7531597fc905a1a9c821eda705dbdcfafdce32385839b.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$ lies in the $3$rd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\pi +{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi +0.429\\,8 \\\\  & ≈3.571\\,4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}≈5.853\\,4\\cdot 3.571\\,4=20.9\n$$\n\nrounded to one decimal place." 13194139534150 true] [17592186278901 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278902 13194139534150 true] [17592186278901 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278903 13194139534150 true] [17592186278901 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278904 13194139534150 true] [17592186278901 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278905 13194139534150 true] [17592186278901 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278906 13194139534150 true] [17592186278901 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450